[00:00.00]Hello, everyone, and welcome back to Mr. English Channel, where learning English is easy and|大家好，欢迎回到 Mr. English Channel——在这里，学英语既轻松
[00:10.52]fun. I'm Emily.|又有趣。我是 Emily。
[00:12.34]Hello, Emily. Hi, everyone. I'm so glad you're joining us for another great conversation|你好，Emily。大家好。很高兴你们又来和我们一起
[00:17.50]today.|聊一场。
[00:18.26]I'm really happy, too, especially because I actually woke up with so much energy today.|我也很开心，尤其因为今天醒来时我精力特别充沛。
[00:24.80]It feels wonderful.|感觉真好。
[00:26.54]Oh, yeah? That's always a great feeling to have.|哦，是吗？这种感觉总是很棒。
[00:29.28]I have my big mug of hot coffee right here, so I'm finally awake now.|我手边就是一大杯热咖啡，现在总算清醒了。
[00:34.66]I see that. You always have that giant coffee mug.|我看到了。你总有那个巨大的咖啡杯。
[00:38.60]I just had some water and a little bit of green tea this morning.|我今天早上只喝了点水和一点绿茶。
[00:42.36]Green tea's nice, but I really need my dark coffee first thing in the morning.|绿茶是不错，但我一早起来就必须来杯浓咖啡。
[00:47.50]Did you do something differently today to have so much extra energy?|你今天是不是做了什么不一样的事，才这么有精神？
[00:50.68]I did, actually. I've been trying to change how I start my day.|还真有。我一直在试着改变自己开始一天的方式。
[00:55.72]I realized my mornings were just getting too rushed and stressful.|我发现自己早上变得太赶、太紧张了。
[01:00.62]I totally understand that.|我完全理解。
[01:02.54]Rushing around your house trying to find your keys or your shoes is the absolute worst way to start the day.|在家里到处翻找钥匙或鞋子，是开始一天最糟糕的方式。
[01:08.50]Exactly.|正是。
[01:09.54]So I decided to create a completely new productive morning routine.|所以我决定给自己设计一套全新的高效晨间流程。
[01:14.72]It's already making a huge difference for me.|它已经给我带来很大改变了。
[01:18.00]That's awesome.|太棒了。
[01:19.18]I'd love to hear about what you're doing now.|我很想听听你现在是怎么做的。
[01:21.02]And you know, if you guys stick around until the end of our chat today, you're going to pick up all the natural vocabulary you need to describe your own daily habits perfectly in English.|另外，如果你们今天听到最后，就能学到描述自己日常习惯所需的全部自然英语说法。
[01:31.16]For sure. It's such an important topic because we all have morning habits.|当然。这个话题很重要，因为我们都有早晨的习惯。
[01:36.32]So the very first thing I changed was my alarm clock.|我改变的第一件事就是闹钟。
[01:40.06]Oh no, please don't tell me you wake up at four in the morning now.|哦不，别告诉我你现在早上四点就起床。
[01:43.84]I really don't think I could ever do that.|我觉得我绝对做不到。
[01:46.12]No, no, not four. But I do wake up about 45 minutes earlier than I used to.|不不，不是四点。但确实比过去早起大概 45 分钟。
[01:52.68]I get up at six instead of almost seven.|我六点起，以前快七点才起。
[01:56.64]That's still pretty early. But I guess waking up early gives you a chance to actually enjoy the morning quietly.|那也挺早的。不过我想，早起能让你有机会安静地享受早晨。
[02:03.02]That's exactly why I do it. The house is completely quiet.|这正是我早起的原因。家里完全安静，
[02:06.88]I don't have to talk to anyone yet. And I can just wake up slowly and peacefully.|不用跟任何人说话，我可以慢慢地、平静地醒来。
[02:12.28]That sounds really nice. Sometimes I hit the snooze button three or four times and then I'm running late.|听起来真好。我有时会按三四次「再睡一会儿」，然后就迟到了。
[02:18.80]I used to do that every single day. Hitting snooze feels good for five minutes, but then you panic.|我以前天天这样。按「再睡一会儿」爽五分钟，然后你就慌了。
[02:27.28]Exactly. You wake up in a total panic. So after you get up at six, what's the very first thing you do?|正是。醒来时慌得不行。那你六点起床后，第一件事做什么？
[02:34.18]The very first thing is making the bed. Before I even leave the bedroom, I fix my pillows and pull up the blanket.|第一件事是铺床。还没出卧室，我就把枕头摆好、被子拉平。
[02:42.10]Really? You make the bed immediately?|真的？你马上就把床铺好？
[02:44.94]I usually just leave it messy and think about doing it later in the afternoon.|我一般就让它乱着，想着下午再收拾。
[02:49.46]I used to do that too, but making the bed only takes two minutes,|我以前也这样，但铺床只要两分钟，
[02:53.78]and it feels like a small victory right away.|而且马上就有种小小的胜利感。
[02:56.76]That makes sense.|有道理。
[02:57.96]It's like you've already accomplished one task,|就像你已经完成了一件事，
[03:00.20]so it gives you a little momentum for the rest of the day.|于是就有了一点推动力，支撑你一整天。
[03:03.00]Exactly. It builds discipline.|正是。它能培养自律。
[03:05.38]Plus, when you come back to your room at night, it looks so clean and relaxing.|而且晚上回到房间时，看起来又干净又舒服。
[03:10.30]That's very true.|太对了。
[03:12.16]Falling into a nicely made bed at the end of a long day is the best feeling.|忙完一天后躺进铺得整整齐齐的床，感觉最好。
[03:16.90]So you make your bed, and then what?|那铺完床，然后呢？
[03:19.42]Then I go straight to the kitchen.|然后我直接去厨房，
[03:21.66]But not for coffee or tea yet.|但不是为了咖啡或茶。
[03:24.14]First, I drink a really large glass of water.|先喝一大杯水。
[03:27.68]Just plain water?|就白水？
[03:29.34]I know that's super healthy, but it's hard for me to remember to do that when I'm still sleepy.|我知道这特别健康，但还困着的时候我很难想起来。
[03:34.62]It's so important, though.|不过这真的很重要。
[03:36.30]We sleep for seven or eight hours, so our bodies are really dehydrated when we wake up.|我们睡了七八个小时，醒来时身体其实很缺水。
[03:42.66]Right. You haven't had anything to drink all night.|对，一整晚什么都没喝。
[03:45.66]Does drinking water actually help you wake up and feel alert?|喝水真能帮你清醒、变得机敏吗？
[03:49.78]It really does. It feels refreshing, and it kind of turns my brain on.|真的能。感觉很清爽，像是把大脑「打开」了。
[03:54.76]Sometimes I add a little slice of fresh lemon, too.|有时我还会加一片新鲜柠檬。
[03:58.26]Oh, lemon water is great. I should probably try doing that instead of grabbing my coffee immediately.|哦，柠檬水很好。我大概该试试这个，而不是一上来就抓咖啡。
[04:04.18]You definitely should try it.|你确实该试试。
[04:06.46]Even just one glass makes a big difference.|哪怕就一杯，效果也差很多。
[04:10.10]After my water, I like to do a little bit of morning exercise.|喝完水，我喜欢做一点晨间运动。
[04:14.90]Wow, you're really productive now.|哇，你现在真高效。
[04:17.42]What kind of exercise are we talking about?|说的是哪种运动？
[04:19.74]Like lifting heavy weights in the living room?|在客厅举重吗？
[04:22.50]Definitely not.|绝对不是。
[04:23.64]I just do some light stretching on the floor,|我就在地上做些轻度拉伸，
[04:26.84]or maybe I take a short walk outside in the neighborhood.|或者去小区里散一小会儿步。
[04:31.02]A morning walk sounds really nice.|晨间散步听起来真好。
[04:32.94]The air is always so fresh and cool early in the morning before the traffic starts.|清晨车流还没起来的时候，空气总是又新鲜又凉爽。
[04:38.28]It is. Just moving my body for about 15 minutes helps me shake off the sleepiness.|确实。只要活动大约 15 分钟，就能帮我赶走困意，
[04:44.76]It gets the blood flowing.|让血液流动起来。
[04:46.48]I really like that phrase, gets the blood flowing.|我很喜欢这个说法，「gets the blood flowing」。
[04:49.86]It just means waking up your body and getting your energy up.|意思就是唤醒身体、把精力提起来。
[04:53.80]Exactly. You don't have to run a marathon.|正是。你不需要去跑马拉松，
[04:56.84]Just a gentle walk or stretching your arms and legs is absolutely perfect.|轻轻散个步，或者伸展一下手脚，就非常好了。
[05:02.94]I feel like if I exercised in the morning, I'd be really hungry right after.|我觉得如果我早上运动，之后会特别饿。
[05:08.38]Do you eat breakfast next?|你接下来吃早饭吗？
[05:10.04]I do. Breakfast is my favorite part of the morning.|吃。早饭是我早上最喜欢的部分。
[05:13.70]I always make sure to have a really healthy, balanced breakfast.|我一定会吃一顿很健康、很均衡的早餐。
[05:18.34]I usually just grab a piece of toast or a banana on my way out the door.|我一般出门时抓一片吐司或者一根香蕉。
[05:22.68]What does a balanced breakfast look like for you?|你的均衡早餐是什么样的？
[05:25.46]Well, I try to have some protein and fruit.|我会尽量摄入一些蛋白质和水果。
[05:28.48]So maybe some scrambled eggs with a piece of whole wheat toast and some fresh berries.|比如炒蛋配一片全麦吐司，再加些新鲜浆果。
[05:35.38]That sounds delicious.|听起来很好吃。
[05:36.96]Scrambled eggs are great because they're fast to cook, but they keep you full for a long time.|炒蛋很好，做起来快，还能让你饱很久。
[05:42.12]Exactly.|正是。
[05:43.18]Or if I want something sweet, I'll make a warm bowl of oatmeal with sliced bananas and a little bit of honey.|或者想吃甜的，我就煮一碗热燕麦粥，加香蕉片和一点蜂蜜。
[05:51.28]Oatmeal is so comforting.|燕麦粥特别暖心。
[05:53.04]It really warms you up on a chilly morning.|在冷飕飕的早晨真的能把你暖起来。
[05:55.80]Do you finally get to drink your tea now?|现在终于能喝茶了吗？
[05:58.44]Yes. While I eat my breakfast, I have my hot green tea.|对。吃早饭时，我喝我的热绿茶。
[06:03.38]That's my quiet time to just sit and enjoy the delicious food.|那是我安静坐着、享受美食的时间。
[06:07.98]That honestly sounds like a perfect morning.|说实话，听起来是个完美的早晨。
[06:10.64]It's calm, you're eating good food, and you aren't rushing at all.|很平静，吃着好东西，一点都不赶。
[06:14.46]It's the best. And speaking of things that are great,|太棒了。说到很棒的事，
[06:17.78]we have so many people listening right now who are improving their English every day.|现在有很多听众每天都在提升英语。
