[06:25.64]And hey, if you're enjoying our chat about morning routines today, please hit that like button and subscribe to the channel.|嘿，如果你喜欢今天关于晨间流程的聊天，请点赞并订阅频道。
[06:32.18]Yes, it really helps us out.|对，这真的帮到我们很多。
[06:34.16]And leave a quick comment below telling us what you usually eat for breakfast.|也请在下面留言，告诉我们你早餐一般吃什么。
[06:38.40]We love reading your answers.|我们很喜欢看你们的回答。
[06:40.82]Definitely.|当然。
[06:41.88]Sharing this video with a friend who's also learning English is an awesome way to practice together, too.|把视频分享给也在学英语的朋友，也是一起练习的好方法。
[06:47.02]So true.|太对了。
[06:48.28]Okay, so after I finish my delicious breakfast, I take a few minutes for planning the day.|好，吃完美味的早餐后，我会花几分钟规划这一天。
[06:54.52]Planning the day.|规划一天。
[06:56.16]Do you use an app on your smartphone for that, or do you prefer writing things down on paper?|你是用手机 App，还是更喜欢写在纸上？
[07:01.32]I actually prefer using a real paper agenda or a small notebook.|我其实更喜欢用纸质日程本或者小笔记本。
[07:06.56]Writing things down with a pen helps me remember them better.|用笔写下来，能帮我记得更牢。
[07:09.98]I totally agree with that.|我完全同意。
[07:11.82]There's something about physically writing a to-do list that makes the tasks feel more real and organized.|亲手写待办清单，会让任务感觉更真实、更有条理。
[07:17.40]Right?|对吧？
[07:17.96]I just write down the top three or four things I absolutely need to get done that day.|我只写下当天必须完成的最重要的三四件事。
[07:22.82]It keeps me focused.|这样能让我保持专注。
[07:24.94]That's a very smart strategy.|很聪明的策略。
[07:26.48]If the list is too long, it can feel overwhelming before you even start working.|清单太长的话，还没开始做就觉得压得慌。
[07:31.30]Exactly.|正是。
[07:32.16]I just focus on the main priorities.|我只关注最主要的几件事。
[07:35.16]Now, you asked about using my smartphone, and that leads to my next big rule.|刚才你问到用手机，这就引出我的下一条大原则。
[07:40.58]Oh boy, I have a feeling I know what you're going to say.|哦天，我大概能猜到你要说什么。
[07:43.84]Let me guess, you don't look at your phone at all.|让我猜猜——你根本不看手机。
[07:47.38]You guessed it.|猜对了。
[07:48.98]Avoiding the phone is a massive part of my new routine.|不碰手机，是我新流程里很重要的一环。
[07:52.82]I don't check it for the first hour of the day.|一天里的第一个小时我不看手机。
[07:56.04]That's so hard to do.|这太难做到了。
[07:57.98]I feel like my automatic habit is to grab my phone from the nightstand the second I open my eyes.|我好像已经形成条件反射，一睁眼就从床头柜上抓手机。
[08:03.62]A lot of people do that.|很多人都这样。
[08:04.94]But if you immediately check social media or read emails, your brain starts reacting to other people's problems.|但如果你立刻刷社交媒体或看邮件，大脑就开始对别人的问题做出反应。
[08:13.52]Wow, that's a really interesting way to look at it.|哇，这个角度很有意思。
[08:16.52]You're reacting instead of just starting your day peacefully on your own terms.|你是在被动反应，而不是按自己的方式平静地开始一天。
[08:21.40]Exactly.|正是。
[08:22.44]You see a stressful news story or an urgent email from your boss,|你看到一条让人紧张的新闻，或者老板发来的紧急邮件，
[08:27.16]and suddenly your calm morning is completely gone.|你平静的早晨瞬间就没了。
[08:31.10]That happens to me all the time.|我经常这样。
[08:33.22]I read one work email while I'm still in bed, and my stress levels just shoot straight up.|还躺在床上读一封工作邮件，压力就直线上升。
[08:39.28]Yep, so I keep my phone in another room while I sleep.|对，所以我睡觉时把手机放在另一个房间。
[08:43.22]I don't even look at a screen until my whole routine is finished.|整套流程做完之前，我连屏幕都不看。
[08:47.32]That takes some serious discipline.|这需要相当的自律。
[08:49.86]But since you aren't looking at your phone, what do you do with that extra quiet time?|但既然不看手机，那段多出来的安静时间你做什么？
[08:54.52]Well, instead of scrolling on social media, I spend a few minutes reading,|我不刷社交媒体，而是花几分钟读书，
[08:59.68]just a physical book or a printed article.|就是纸质书或打印出来的文章。
[09:03.34]Reading in the morning sounds very relaxing.|早上读书听起来很放松。
[09:05.72]Do you read fiction, like a novel, or do you prefer something else?|你读小说这类虚构作品，还是更喜欢别的？
[09:10.28]I usually prefer reading something that gives me a good perspective for the day,|我一般喜欢读能给我一天带来好视角的东西，
[09:14.86]so I'll often read a few chapters from the Bible.|所以我常读几章圣经。
[09:18.70]That's a wonderful habit.|这是个很好的习惯。
[09:20.66]Taking that quiet time for your faith really helps center your mind before the day gets busy and loud.|为信仰留出这段安静时间，能在一天变得忙碌嘈杂之前帮你收拢心神。
[09:26.34]It really does.|确实。
[09:27.34]It brings me a lot of peace.|它带给我很多安宁。
[09:30.06]If I'm not reading that, I might read a short article about personal growth or history.|如果不读那个，我可能会读一篇关于个人成长或历史的短文。
[09:35.74]Just learning something new for a few minutes?|就是花几分钟学点新东西？
[09:38.02]It's like a small workout for your brain before you start your actual job.|就像正式开始工作前给大脑做个小热身。
[09:42.26]Exactly.|正是。
[09:43.32]It's so much better than watching funny videos online and wasting 20 minutes without even realizing it.|这比刷搞笑视频、不知不觉浪费 20 分钟好太多了。
[09:50.68]I'm definitely guilty of doing that.|我就经常这么干。
[09:53.42]It's so easy to get distracted by short videos and lose track of time.|短视频太容易让人分心、忘记时间了。
[09:57.82]We all do it, but replacing that habit with a real book just feels more rewarding.|我们都会这样，但把那个习惯换成读真书，感觉更有收获。
[10:04.02]After I read, it's finally time to get ready for the day.|读完之后，终于该准备出门了。
[10:07.58]Okay, so this is the part where you take a shower, get dressed, and do all of that normal everyday stuff.|好，这部分就是洗澡、穿衣，做那些日常的事。
[10:13.36]Yep, taking a warm shower is the final step to fully waking up.|对，洗个热水澡是彻底清醒的最后一步。
[10:18.26]Then I get dressed and prepare my bag for work.|然后穿衣，准备上班的包。
[10:21.40]Do you pick out your clothes in the morning or do you choose them the night before?|你是早上挑衣服，还是前一晚就选好？
[10:24.64]I actually choose my outfit the night before.|我其实前一晚就选好衣服。
[10:27.98]It saves me so much time and stops me from standing in front of the closet feeling confused.|这省下很多时间，也免得我站在衣柜前发懵。
[10:34.10]That's a pro tip right there.|这真是高手的窍门。
[10:35.84]Making decisions in the morning can be tough, so doing it at night is brilliant.|早上做决定很难，放到晚上做很聪明。
[10:40.06]It really is. By the time I have my shoes on and my bag packed, I feel completely ready to go.|确实。等我穿好鞋、收拾好包，就完全准备好出发了。
[10:46.84]It sounds like your whole morning is designed to remove stress.|听起来你整个早晨都是为了消除压力而设计的，
[10:50.16]You're just calmly moving from one thing to the next.|你就是平静地从一件事走到下一件事。
[10:53.12]That's the perfect way to describe it.|这个描述太贴切了。
[10:55.02]And the final piece of the routine is leaving home with a positive mindset.|整套流程的最后一步，是带着积极的心态出门。
[11:00.08]A positive mindset is so important.|积极的心态太重要了。
[11:02.54]How do you make sure you stay positive right as you walk out the front door?|你怎么保证走出家门时依然保持积极？
[11:05.98]I just take one deep breath, smile, and tell myself that it's going to be a good day, no matter what happens.|我就深吸一口气、笑一笑，告诉自己：不管发生什么，今天都会是美好的一天。
[11:14.42]I love that. You're choosing your attitude before the world can decide it for you. It's very empowering.|我喜欢这个。你在世界替你决定之前，就先选好了自己的态度，非常有力量。
[11:20.38]Exactly. Even if there's heavy traffic or it's raining, I already had a peaceful morning, so I can handle it easily.|正是。哪怕堵车或下雨，我已经拥有一个平静的早晨，所以轻松就能应对。
[11:29.30]It really shows how our daily habits shape our whole lives.|这确实说明日常习惯如何塑造我们的整个人生。
[11:33.60]If you start calm, you stay calm throughout the day.|平静地开始，就能平静地过完一天。
[11:36.90]You said that perfectly.|说得太好了。
[11:38.96]You know, we've used a lot of really great phrases today while talking about all these daily habits.|你知道，今天聊这些日常习惯时，我们用到了不少很好的短语。
[11:45.28]We definitely have.|确实。
[11:46.76]Let's look back at a few of them really quickly because they're super useful for daily conversations.|我们快速回顾几个，因为它们在日常对话里超级实用。
[11:52.10]Good idea.|好主意。
[11:52.88]One phrase I used earlier was hitting the snooze button.|我前面用过的一个短语是「hitting the snooze button」。
[11:57.18]That's a very common thing people say in America.|这是美国人非常常说的说法。
[12:00.62]Oh, yeah.|哦对。
[12:01.60]The snooze button is that button on your alarm clock that gives you five or ten more minutes of sleep.|「Snooze button」就是闹钟上那个让你再多睡五到十分钟的按钮。
[12:07.42]Exactly.|正是。
[12:08.58]So if you say, I hit snooze three times this morning, everyone knows exactly what you mean.|所以你说「I hit snooze three times this morning.」，大家都明白你的意思：
[12:15.08]You delayed waking up.|你把起床往后拖了。
[12:17.56]Another good one we mentioned was getting the blood flowing.|我们提到的另一个好短语是「getting the blood flowing」。
[12:21.06]You said that when you were talking about your morning walk.|那是你聊晨间散步时说的。
[12:24.08]Yes. It just means doing some light physical activity to wake up your body and feel much more energetic.|对。意思是做些轻度活动来唤醒身体，让自己更有精神。
[12:31.36]Like, doing some quick stretches gets the blood flowing.|比如，快速拉伸一下能「让血液流动起来」。
[12:34.82]It's a really natural idiom to use when talking about light exercise.|谈论轻度运动时，这是个非常自然的说法。
[12:39.32]For sure. I also talked about picking out my clothes.|当然。我还提到了「picking out my clothes」。
[12:43.58]To pick out just means to choose or select something from a group.|「Pick out」就是从一堆里挑选、挑出。
[12:47.94]Right. You could say, I need to pick out a nice shirt for the party.|对。你可以说「I need to pick out a nice shirt for the party.」
[12:52.12]It's much more common in daily conversation than saying select.|在日常对话里，它比说「select」常见得多。
[12:56.88]Totally. And the last one was checking my phone.|完全对。最后一个是「checking my phone」。
[13:00.62]We don't usually say looking at my phone when we mean reading messages or emails.|想说看消息或邮件时，我们一般不说「looking at my phone」，
[13:06.46]Yep. We say checking. I'm checking my emails or I'm checking social media.|对，我们说「checking」：「I'm checking my emails.」或者「I'm checking social media.」
[13:11.94]It implies a quick look for new updates.|它暗含「快速看一眼有没有新动态」。
[13:15.04]Exactly. Those are all fantastic everyday expressions.|正是。这些都是极好的日常表达。
[13:19.06]but sometimes when people talk about their routines, they make a few small mistakes.|不过有时人们聊自己的作息时，会犯几个小错误。
[13:26.10]That's very true. I hear a couple of the same mistakes pretty often.|确实。有几个错误我经常听到。
[13:30.38]Let's look at how to make those sentences sound much more natural.|我们来看看怎么让这些句子听起来自然得多。
[13:33.84]Sounds great. Here's a very common one.|好。先说一个很常见的。
[13:37.04]Sometimes someone will say, I take my breakfast at 7 o'clock.|有人会说「I take my breakfast at 7 o'clock.」
[13:41.58]Right. I hear that a lot.|对，我常听到。
[13:43.52]In some languages, you use the verb take for meals, but in English, we just don't do that.|有些语言里吃饭用「take」，但英语不这么用。
[13:49.04]Exactly. To sound more natural, you should use the verb have or eat.|正是。想更自然，应该用「have」或「eat」。
[13:54.78]So you say, I have breakfast at 7 o'clock.|所以说「I have breakfast at 7 o'clock.」
[13:58.58]Or I eat breakfast at 7.|或者「I eat breakfast at 7.」
[14:00.78]Both of those sound perfectly natural to an American speaker.|这两句在美国人听来都完全自然。
[14:03.90]Here's another one.|再来一个。
[14:05.38]Sometimes people say, I make a shower in the morning before work.|有人会说「I make a shower in the morning before work.」
[14:09.62]Ah, yes. The verb make is tricky for a lot of people.|啊对。「make」这个动词让很多人头疼。
[14:13.32]But for showers and baths, we always use the verb take.|但洗澡、泡澡，我们一定用「take」。
[14:16.96]Right. So the natural way to say it is, I take a shower in the morning.|对。自然的说法是「I take a shower in the morning.」
[14:22.12]It's a small change, but it sounds so much better.|改动很小，但听起来好太多了。
[14:25.86]Definitely. One more mistake I hear is when people say, I get up of the bed.|绝对。还有一个错误是有人说「I get up of the bed.」
[14:30.72]They add that little word of.|他们多加了「of」这个词。
[14:33.18]Yes, that's completely unnecessary. You just need to say, I get out of bed.|对，完全没必要。只要说「I get out of bed.」就行，
[14:38.66]Or simply, I get up.|或者简单说「I get up.」
[14:41.12]Exactly. I get out of bed at 6.|正是。「I get out of bed at 6.」
[14:43.56]It flows much more smoothly and sounds just like a native speaker talking.|说起来顺畅多了，听起来就像母语者在说话。
[14:48.08]I love fixing those tiny details.|我很喜欢纠正这些小细节。
[14:50.74]It really boosts your speaking confidence.|这确实能提升开口的自信。
[14:53.60]Now, let's put everything we've talked about into a quick real-life situation.|现在，把我们聊过的都放进一个简短的现实场景里。
[14:58.92]Good idea.|好主意。
[14:59.82]Let's imagine we're co-workers arriving at the office on a Monday morning and we're just catching up by the coffee machine.|想象我们是同事，周一早上到公司，在咖啡机旁闲聊。
[15:05.80]Perfect. I'll start.|太好了。我先来。
[15:08.12]Hey, Paul. Good morning. How was your weekend?|嘿，Paul。早上好。周末过得怎么样？
[15:11.16]Good morning, Emily.|早上好，Emily。
[15:11.94]It was great, but I'm pretty tired today.|挺好的，不过我今天挺累的。
[15:15.60]I definitely hit the snooze button a few too many times this morning.|今早我确实多按了好几次「再睡一会儿」。
[15:20.50]Oh no.|哦不。
[15:21.70]Did you have to rush to get here on time?|你是不是得赶着才准时到？
[15:24.30]I really did.|真的。
[15:25.76]I barely had time to take a shower.|我几乎没时间洗澡。
[15:28.24]And I didn't even eat breakfast before leaving the house.|出门前连早饭都没吃。
[15:31.68]You need to start waking up just a little bit earlier.|你得开始早一点起床了。
[15:35.24]I get up at 6 now and I always have time for a healthy breakfast and some green tea.|我现在六点起，总能有时间吃顿健康早餐、喝点绿茶。
[15:40.86]Six in the morning? Wow, you're dedicated. Do you check your emails while you eat your breakfast?|早上六点？哇，你真自律。你吃早饭时会看邮件吗？
[15:47.44]Never. I keep my phone away from the table. I just prefer to plan my day in my notebook|从不。我把手机放得离桌子很远。我更喜欢在本子上规划一天，
[15:53.14]so I know exactly what I need to do.|这样我清楚知道自己要做什么。
[15:55.74]That sounds incredibly peaceful. Maybe I'll try to pick out my clothes tonight|听起来特别宁静。也许今晚我也试着把衣服挑好，
[16:00.90]so tomorrow morning is a little easier for me.|这样明早能轻松一点。
[16:03.74]You should. Just a few small changes can give you a completely positive mindset for the whole day.|你该试试。几个小小的改变，就能让你一整天都保持积极的心态。
[16:10.46]You're right. I'm going to try it.|你说得对。我要试试。
[16:13.02]Well, thanks for the advice, Emily. Let's get to work.|好，谢谢你的建议，Emily。我们干活去吧。
[16:16.38]That was great.|太棒了。
[16:18.04]You see how naturally all of those phrases fit right into a normal office conversation?|看到那些短语多自然地融进普通办公室对话了吗？
[16:23.64]They really do.|确实。
[16:25.24]When you hear vocabulary in context like that,|当你这样在语境里听到词汇，
[16:27.84]it's so much easier to remember and use in your own life.|记住并在生活中使用就容易多了。
[16:31.48]Absolutely. It just takes a little bit of practice.|绝对。只需要一点练习。
[16:35.24]Creating a morning routine in English is a fantastic way to practice every single day.|用英语搭建晨间流程，是每天都能练习的绝佳方式。
[16:40.82]For sure.|当然。
[16:41.82]When you're making your bed tomorrow, just think to yourself in English,|明天铺床时，试着用英语在心里说：
[16:45.08]I'm making the bed.|「I'm making the bed.」
[16:46.82]It helps so much.|这特别有帮助。
[16:48.08]That's a perfect tip.|这建议太好了。
[16:49.66]Well, we really hope you all enjoyed this conversation today|好，我们真心希望你们喜欢今天的对话，
